  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "City traffic",
  "description": "The cones are the edge of the city and the ball is your car. Everyone drives around town without crashing and without leaving the city. The coach calls out traffic signals: \"Green\" – full speed, \"Red\" – stop with your foot on the ball, \"Reverse\" – drag the ball back with your sole, \"Roundabout\" – turn and go the other way. Make up your own signals with the children.\n\nAfter a while a car thief (without a ball) joins in. The thief tries to steal a car, and whoever loses their ball becomes the new thief. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up so you can see where the space is."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Keep the ball close to your foot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Change direction and pace when someone gets close."
    }
  ],
